  "incremental_mac": {
    "construction": "One HMAC-SHA256 keyed with the 32-byte MAC half of the attachment key runs over the whole stream without reset; after every chunk_size bytes the HMAC of the prefix so far is emitted (the HMAC state continues, it is not re-keyed or reset); at end of stream the HMAC of the whole stream is emitted ONCE MORE, always. So the digest has floor(len/chunk_size)+1 entries of 32 bytes; when len is an exact non-zero multiple of chunk_size the last two entries are equal; an empty stream gives one entry, HMAC(key, empty). Digest = concatenation of the entries. The key used for attachments is the second 32-byte half of the 64-byte attachment key, and the MAC'd stream is the attachment CIPHERTEXT (iv || cbc || mac). signal-cli 0.14.7 neither produces nor checks it (spec section 2.6).",
